        "workup_and_crystallization": "After cooling, purple block crystals; enantiomers 1 and 3 separated by hand under a polarizing microscope.",
        "yield": "0.1709 g, 22.2% based on Gd (for mixed 1 and 3)"
      },
      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "Enantiomer of the Gd4Cr4 cluster (CD opposite to 3). Magnetic data for the 1+3 mixture show antiferromagnetic coupling and a cryogenic magnetocaloric effect with −ΔSm = 18.08 J kg−1 K−1 (34.69 mJ cm−3 K−1) at ~3 K and ΔH = 7 T. SHG of the 1+3 mixture is 0.3 times that of urea.",
        "measurements": [
          {
            "property_type": "magnetic",
